    "created_at": "2019-12-12T21:37:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-12-12T21:37:37Z",
    "body": "It's not terribly complex. we intentionally don't differentiate between a calc or not since https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1577139, though we could re-introduce it...\r\n\r\nThat being said, I think given Firefox is inconsistent, and Blink and WebKit do treat calc-with-percentages the same as percentages, I think I'm with @bfgeek that the esiest thing is for Firefox to change. It kinda sucks, but the behavior for replaced elements has been consistent across all browsers since calc() existed...",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
