    "created_at": "2026-11-05T08:10:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-05T08:10:48Z",
    "body": "IMO it's quite weird if `calc(100% + 0px)` has the quirk but `calc(100% + 1px)` doesn't. Sure, the former resolves to a lone percentage, but it's still using modern syntax, so the argument of limiting quirks to old syntax doesn't hold very strongly.\n\nAnd applying the quirk to `100%` but not `calc(100% + 0px)` would require unnecessary complexity.\n\nThat said, for now I have aligned Servo with Firefox, since the spec says `<percentage>` and there is a WPT subtest about it.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
