    "created_at": "2026-11-14T21:59:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-11-14T21:59:24Z",
    "body": "This is somewhat entangled with #95:\n\n```html\n<!-- quirks -->\n<div style=\"height: 50px; width: 50px\">\n  <div style=\"background: red\">\n    <div style=\"height: 0%; min-height: calc(100% + 1px); background: green\"></div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\nAll browsers including Firefox use the quirk for `min-height: calc(100% + 1px)`: it's 51px tall.\n\nSo then avoiding the quirk if it's `height` the one that has `calc()` seems a bit arbitrary.",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
